ctroplating, and cleaning. In addition, the company provides precision-machined components, weldments, e-beam and laser welded components, precision vacuum and hydrogen brazing, surface treatment technologies, and other proprietary products. It sells and markets its products to equipment OEMs in the semiconductor equipment market. Ichor Holdings, Ltd. was incorporated in 1999 and is headquartered in Fremont, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Philip  Barros | CEO & Director | Age 45 | Compensation: $620,848 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $501K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers. Stock-based compensation of $9K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["Ichor Holdings is a small-cap technology business with a $1.3B market cap on $948M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -10% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -1% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 14% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The company is burning through $6M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, thin -5.9\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on 